{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "weno5_eno1_signed_D1x_interior",
    "description": "Interior-only hybrid WENO5/ENO1 upwind first derivative d u/dx for the level-set REINITIALISATION equation of NCAR fire_behavior (physics/level_set_mod.F90 Advance_ls_reinit, fire_upwinding_reinit = 4), on cartesian_uniform_2d over the block [4, NX-3] x [3, NY-2]. It is stencils/weno5_eno1_D1x_interior with the two changes the reinitialisation makes, and nothing else. (1) THE UPWIND SIDE IS CHOSEN BY A SUPPLIED SIGN FIELD, not by the wind. The propagation scheme forms a_valor = (grad4 u . (wind_u, wind_v)) and takes sgn = a_valor (d4 u/dx); the reinitialisation takes sgn = upwind_sign[i,j] (d4 u/dx), where upwind_sign is fire_behavior's lfn_s0, the smoothed sign S(psi_0) = psi_0 / sqrt(psi_0^2 + dx^2) frozen at the start of the pseudo-time iteration. `upwind_sign` is therefore a FREE NAME the consumer must declare as an [x, y] field, replacing this family's usual `wind_u`/`wind_v` pair (neither of which this stencil references). (2) THE BAND TEST IS SIGNED, NOT ABSOLUTE: this stencil takes ENO1 when u[i,j] >= weno_band_cells * dx, whereas the propagation stencil takes it when |u[i,j]| >= weno_band_cells * dx. That is faithful to the reference code, which writes `if (lfn_curr(i, j) < threshold_hlu)` at level_set_mod.F90:1019, :1039 and :1061 while Calc_tend_ls writes `if (abs (lfn(i, j)) < threshold_hlu)` at :1278 and :1298. The missing abs is almost certainly an oversight -- it puts the whole BURNED INTERIOR, where the level set is large and negative, on the fifth-order branch that is meant for the band around the front -- but it is what the model computes, and a transcription that silently inserted the abs would not reproduce it. Everything else (the Jiang-Shu WENO5 of stencils/weno5_js_upwind_D1, the ENO1 minmod of stencils/eno1_minmod, the fourth-order selector of stencils/central_D1_4_point, the wall-distance test on bdy_eno1_cells, the block bounds) is identical to the propagation sibling. Free names: upwind_sign, bdy_eno1_cells, weno_band_cells, dx, dy.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:stencil",
      "family:finite_difference",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d",
      "op:D",
      "axes:x,y",
      "order:1",
      "stencil_width:7"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Munoz-Esparza, D., Kosovic, B., Jimenez, P. A., & Coen, J. L. (2018). An accurate fire-spread algorithm in the Weather Research and Forecasting model using the level-set method. Journal of Advances in Modeling Earth Systems, 10(4), 908-926. The hybrid WENO5/ENO1 level-set scheme (fire_upwinding = 9) of WRF-Fire / NCAR fire_behavior.",
        "doi": "10.1002/2017MS001108"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Jiang, G.-S., & Shu, C.-W. (1996). Efficient implementation of weighted ENO schemes. Journal of Computational Physics, 126(1), 202-228. The classical WENO5 smoothness indicators beta_k and nonlinear weights w_k = gamma_k/(beta_k + eps)^2.",
        "doi": "10.1006/jcph.1996.0130"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Harten, A., Engquist, B., Osher, S., & Chakravarthy, S. R. (1987). Uniformly high order accurate essentially non-oscillatory schemes, III. Journal of Computational Physics, 71(2), 231-303. ENO stencil selection by smallest divided difference (first-order form: the minmod limiter).",
        "doi": "10.1016/0021-9991(87)90031-3"
      },
      {
        "citation": "NCAR Community Fire Behavior Model (fire_behavior), develop @ eb77580, physics/level_set_mod.F90: Calc_tend_ls, Select_eno, Select_weno5, Select_4th, Select_godunov (case 4), Extrapol_var_at_bdys. The transcribed reference implementation."
      }
    ]
  },
